WEBVTT

1
00:00:09.800 --> 00:00:20.944
Plop! A drop of sweat fell from Jason's forehead.

2
00:00:20.945 --> 00:00:24.259
It landed right on his video game.

3
00:00:24.260 --> 00:00:28.542
"Ugh. It's so hot!"

4
00:00:28.543 --> 00:00:32.098
Mr. Dunn pointed at Jason's game.

5
00:00:32.099 --> 00:00:34.488
"That needs to go away.

6
00:00:34.489 --> 00:00:38.219
We're about to head inside to make some food."

7
00:00:38.220 --> 00:00:43.632
"We're cooking on this hot, hot day?" Jason asked.

8
00:00:43.633 --> 00:00:47.838
"I hope we're not using the oven!" Bobby cried.

9
00:00:47.839 --> 00:00:52.942
Mr. Dunn chuckled. "Don't worry.

10
00:00:52.943 --> 00:00:57.010
We're making cold cucumber pickles.

11
00:00:57.011 --> 00:00:59.468
Perfect for today."

12
00:00:59.469 --> 00:01:01.361
"That's no fun.

13
00:01:01.362 --> 00:01:05.070
Pickles have to sit around in jars for a long time.

14
00:01:05.071 --> 00:01:09.404
We won't get to eat them today!" Jason frowned.

15
00:01:09.405 --> 00:01:13.947
"We're making instant pickles." Mr. Dunn winked.

16
00:01:13.948 --> 00:01:16.362
"Have you ever made those?"

17
00:01:16.363 --> 00:01:18.521
Jason shook his head.

18
00:01:18.522 --> 00:01:20.524
"We should get started.

19
00:01:20.525 --> 00:01:23.459
The process has a few steps.

20
00:01:23.460 --> 00:01:29.148
But I promise they'll be ready to eat by the end of the day."

21
00:01:29.149 --> 00:01:31.809
Mr. Dunn clapped his hands.

22
00:01:31.810 --> 00:01:35.768
"It's pickle time!"

23
00:01:35.769 --> 00:01:38.800
Inside the gym it was still hot.

24
00:01:38.801 --> 00:01:43.013
But Jason was glad there was a fan.

25
00:01:43.014 --> 00:01:49.336
"Look at all those cucumbers!" Ethan cried.

26
00:01:49.337 --> 00:01:54.863
"They're from my garden," Mr. Dunn said proudly.

27
00:01:54.864 --> 00:01:59.610
"So how do we turn cucumbers into pickles?" Izzie asked.

28
00:01:59.611 --> 00:02:06.019
"First choose a cucumber from the basket," said Mr. Dunn.

29
00:02:06.020 --> 00:02:09.628
"Yay! We each get our own!"

30
00:02:09.629 --> 00:02:12.933
Nina picked the smallest one.

31
00:02:12.934 --> 00:02:16.470
"There's a cutting board and knife for each of you.

32
00:02:16.471 --> 00:02:21.244
Carefully slice your cucumbers as thin as possible.

33
00:02:21.245 --> 00:02:30.185
Place the slices in the bowls of salt water," Mr. Dunn instructed.

34
00:02:30.186 --> 00:02:34.436
Jason carefully followed the teacher's instructions.

35
00:02:34.437 --> 00:02:40.813
"We'll leave our slices there and prepare the pickle juice."

36
00:02:40.814 --> 00:02:46.424
Mr. Dunn motioned for everyone to follow him to the next table.

37
00:02:46.425 --> 00:02:52.381
Nina looked confused.

38
00:02:52.382 --> 00:02:57.466
"Pickle juice is the liquid you put pickles in," Jason whispered.

39
00:02:57.467 --> 00:03:00.682
Nina smiled thankfully.

40
00:03:00.683 --> 00:03:15.379
"The juice is eight tablespoons rice vinegar," read Bobby.

41
00:03:15.380 --> 00:03:21.562
"And one and a half tablespoons sugar," Ethan continued.

42
00:03:21.563 --> 00:03:25.976
"Plus one teaspoon salt," Izzie added.

43
00:03:25.977 --> 00:03:37.008
"And four tablespoons of boiling water!" Nina said.

44
00:03:37.009 --> 00:03:40.654
The kids each made their own jar of pickle juice.

45
00:03:40.655 --> 00:03:45.557
When they were done, Mr. Dunn reminded them about their cucumbers.

46
00:03:45.558 --> 00:03:48.070
"It's time to drain them.

47
00:03:48.071 --> 00:03:56.902
One at a time now at the sink."

48
00:03:56.903 --> 00:03:59.059
"Here's the fun part.

49
00:03:59.060 --> 00:04:04.465
Squeeze the extra water out of the slices with your hands.

50
00:04:04.466 --> 00:04:07.270
Just like you're wringing a towel.

51
00:04:07.271 --> 00:04:10.880
Grab a bunch and squeeze.

52
00:04:10.881 --> 00:04:15.913
Then pat them dry with a paper towel," said Mr. Dunn.

53
00:04:15.914 --> 00:04:20.310
Jason grabbed a handful of cucumber slices and squeezed.

54
00:04:20.311 --> 00:04:24.011
The cucumbers felt cold in Jason's hands.

55
00:04:24.012 --> 00:04:29.283
It was the first time he felt cool all day.

56
00:04:29.284 --> 00:04:33.752
He patted them dry, and then turned to Mr. Dunn.

57
00:04:33.753 --> 00:04:38.363
"Now is it time to put the cucumbers in the pickle juice?" he asked.

58
00:04:38.364 --> 00:04:49.035
Mr. Dunn nodded. "Sure is."

59
00:04:49.036 --> 00:04:51.563
"It's twelve o'clock now.

60
00:04:51.564 --> 00:04:54.496
Our pickles will be ready at three."

61
00:04:54.497 --> 00:04:58.953
Mr. Dunn looked around at the hot, sweaty faces.

62
00:04:58.954 --> 00:05:05.172
"That's just enough time for a quick trip to the air-conditioned town library."

63
00:05:05.173 --> 00:05:09.071
"Hooray!" Everyone cheered.

64
00:05:09.072 --> 00:05:12.139
Later the campers returned to the gym.

65
00:05:12.140 --> 00:05:14.924
The pickles were waiting.

66
00:05:14.925 --> 00:05:20.494
The campers drained the juice and then grabbed forks.

67
00:05:20.495 --> 00:05:26.088
A cold mouthful of pickles tickled as it slid down Jason's throat.

68
00:05:26.089 --> 00:05:37.597
"Yum! Instant pickles are my new favorite food!"

69
00:05:37.598 --> 00:05:49.208
[caption_out@
